207 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 130 0 R
/E (On 7 July, three tankers were attacked in the Strait of Hormuz. The US revoked the waiver on its sanctions of Iran's oil exports, and Trump declared the June truce "over." Marine war-risk premiums jumped from about 2% to 3% of hull value within a day, Hormuz transit has come to a standstill again. Companies moving oil, gas or containers through the Gulf should hold war-risk cover, buffer stocks and force-majeure provisions rather than unwind them, and budget freight and insurance around a strait that can re-close at short notice.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
