210 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 130 0 R
/E (On 28 June, the IRGC struck the US Ali Al Salem airbase in Kuwait and US Fifth Fleet sites in Bahrain, where a missile damaged a residential building in Muharraq near the international airport; a vessel in the Gulf was hit, killing a Qatari civilian. The attacks brought the war back onto GCC soil and prompted UAE adviser Anwar Gargash to call for a unified Gulf security stance. Firms with staff, aviation exposure or fixed operations across Kuwait and Bahrain should review business-continuity and evacuation plans and expect intermittent airport and airspace disruption.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
211 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 130 0 R
/E (UAE ACCELERATES 'ZERO HORMUZ' ROUTING \(LOGISTICS\))
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
212 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 130 0 R
/E (In early July, the UAE stepped up its plan to cut dependence on the Strait of Hormuz toward zero, centred on expanding its Gulf-of-Oman ports \(Fujairah, Khor Fakkan, Dibba\) and a second crude pipeline to Fujairah that would lift bypass capacity above 3.5 million b/d. Gulf ports risk ceding transshipment share to India and Sri Lanka as cargo reroutes. Shippers and traders should build longer lead times and transshipment costs into Gulf supply chains and treat the eastern seaboard, not Hormuz, as the region's growth capacity. But note that this shift is years off \(the second Fujairah pipeline is due only in 2027\) and that the Emirati eastern seaboard is itself within Iranian missile range.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
