/P 132 0 R
/E (The 17 June truce nominally opened a 60-day negotiating window \(to ~16 August\) but was declared "over" on 7 July. Whether talks resume or formally collapse is the main swing factor for Q3 freight, insurance and fuel costs: a credible return to negotiations is the cue to lock in forward cover before rates ease, while a collapse means holding buffer stocks and war-risk cover and pricing contracts off a strait that stays shut.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
